WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:06.210
Huawei's chief financial officer was granted
bail of ten million dollars after three days

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:11.870
of hearings in Vancouver. Meng Wanzhou will
have to turn over her passports, wear an ankel

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:16.219
bracelet, and she will confined at night to
her home in Vancouver.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:21.660
Meng is a often viewed as a national heroine
in China, so her release after over a week

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:27.390
in detentionwas a relief to many in Beijing.
I feel happy. It`s a victory for the national

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:33.150
enterprise. Although it`s only a bail, I still
hope all the sanctions on Huawei could be

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:38.149
cancelled. It is important that we have fair
international competition. Sanctions only

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:43.590
on China is not fairness.
Still, the prospect of the Meng being used

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:49.210
as a bargaining chip in trade negotiations
between China and the US increased, as US

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.899
president Trump said he would intervene in
the case if it was in America's interest.

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:59.320
Hours before the bail hearing, a former Canadian
diplomat was arrested in Beijing, presumably

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:05.400
in retaliation for Meng's arrest. Canada's
government is still collecting details.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.870
We are aware of the situation of the Canadian
detained in China. We have been in direct

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:17.360
contact with the Chinese, Chinese diplomats
and representatives. We are engaged on the

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.530
file which we take very seriously and we are
of course providing consular assistance to

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:26.130
the family.
Markets in Asia closed higher after Meng was

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.560
released, as investors' eased their fears
about the trade battle among the world's two

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.810
top economies.

